Package: POLARIS
Title: Concordance-Aware Integration of Paired Single-Cell Multiomic Data
Version: 0.99.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ziqi", "Fu", email = "ziqi_fu@hsph.harvard.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: POLARIS is a concordance-aware framework for paired single-cell
    multiomic assays that profile two modalities in the same cells, such as
    RNA with ATAC or RNA with surface protein. From a single closed-form
    spectral decomposition it returns a per-cell cross-modality concordance
    score, a joint cell embedding that preserves structure supported by either
    modality, and an induced cross-modal feature embedding that scores
    candidate regulatory element to gene and protein to gene pairs. Feature
    linkage scores carry a closed-form leave-one-cell-out standard error and a
    genomic-distance-aware z-statistic, so candidate pairs can be ranked with
    uncertainty rather than by magnitude alone. The feature embedding can be
    recomputed on any subset of cells without refitting, giving cell-type
    specific linkage from one global fit. POLARIS runs on CPU and scales to
    tens of thousands of cells.
